                  <decoDesc>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d1"><locus target="#iv" facs="002"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1035HolyMan">Holy Man Portrait</ref> <name ref="PRS4306GabraMa"/> surrounded by lions and leopards with a bird pecking his eye</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d2"><locus target="#iir" facs="002"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1114Gabriel">AT1114Gabriel</ref> and the Three Youths in the Fiery Furnace</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d3"><locus target="#iiv" facs="003"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1035HolyMan">Holy Man Portrait</ref> <name ref="PRS9150TaklaHa"/> standing for prayer</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d4"><locus target="#ivr" facs="004"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1033Ascension">Ascension of Jesus</ref></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d5"><locus target="#ivv" facs="005"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1031VirginAndChild">Virgin and Child</ref></desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="miniature" xml:id="d6"><locus target="#25r" facs="028"/><desc><ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1077ArchangelMichael">AT1077ArchangelMichael</ref> standing over a demon</desc></decoNote>
                    <decoNote type="frame" xml:id="d7">
                      Decorative designs: <locus target="#1r" facs="003"/>, ornamental band;
                      multiple full stops used as section dividers throughout (e.g. <locus target="#3v #4v #5v" facs="006 007 008"/>;
                      <locus target="#44r #74v #79r #82r #87r #88r #90r #94r #118v #119r #121v #148v" facs="046 077 081 084 089 090 092 096 121 121 124 151"/>, line/lines of alternating red and black dots;
                      <locus target="#77v #79v #81r" facs="080 082 083"/>, line of black dots)</decoNote>
                  </decoDesc>
                  <additions><list>
                    <item xml:id="e1"><desc><locus target="#ir" facs="001"/>Contains the date <date calendar="ethiopian">Ḥamle 6, 19[1]5 E.C.</date>. The space for the tens digit has been prepared for a number, but no number has been added (<foreign xml:lang="gez">፲፱፻[ ]፭ ዓመት፡ ሐምሌ፡ ፮ቀን፡</foreign>)</desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="a1"><desc type="OwnershipNote"><locus target="#10r" facs="012">f. 10r and passim</locus> mention the owner Wäldä Giyorgis (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ወልደ፡ ጊዮርጊስ፡</foreign>)</desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="a2"><desc><locus target="#138r #144r" facs="140 146"/> mentions <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6876Matewos">Mātewos X</persName></desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="a3"><desc><locus target="#144r #144v #145v" facs="146 147 148"/> mentions <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10671Zawditu">Zawditu</persName></desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="a4"><desc>Every so often in the book, a section of text is written in small writing (e.g., <locus target="#43v #44r #67 #68r" facs="046 070"/>).
                    These contain collections of chants. </desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="e2"><desc>In most places where the departed are to be mentioned by name, a blank space is left in the manuscript (e.g., <locus target="#38v" facs="041"/>)</desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="e3"><desc>Numbered quires 2–18.</desc></item>
                    <item xml:id="e4"><desc>
                      Scribal intervention:
                      words of text are written interlinearly,  <locus target="#7r #8v #14v #35v #45r" facs="009 011 017 038 047"/>, etc.);
                      text has been removed (<locus target="#6v #23r #44v #45r #51v" facs="009 025 047 047 054"/>, etc.)</desc>
                    </item>
                  </list></additions>

                  <bindingDesc>
                    <binding xml:id="binding" contemporary="true">
                      <decoNote xml:id="b1">Parchment, four Coptic chain stitches attached with bridle attachments to rough-hewn boards of the traditional wood covered with tooled leather, fabric visible between the turn-ins.</decoNote>
                      <decoNote xml:id="b2" type="bindingMaterial">
                        <material key="parchment"/>
                        <material key="wood"/>
                        <material key="leather"/>
                        <material key="textile"/>
                      </decoNote>
                    </binding>
